    {
      "id": "-5kt9WtAyMoJ1nb01wWar",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3910.917822756835,
      "y": 2898.7288493871292,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1871440612,
      "version": 1109,
      "versionNonce": 558375689,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795014337424,
      "created": 1794751597369,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NFR Explain : \n1) 99.99% Availability -> using db failover, cache heavy read data like\nsubscription status, fallback again we can use db read replica\n2) Strong Consistency, CP -> use ACID transaction, fail closed if service crash/\ndown\n3) <100MS, check status, <200ms buy subscription p95 -> We reduce most RPC\ncall between internal service, and we will do load test after implementing the\nservice since latency is difficult to estimate as we have external RPC call.\n4) Durability (outbox event will make sure kafka can retry, and our worker and\nservice will do retry after timeout)\n5) Reliability (No duplicate payment, or subscription) -> Idempotency key from\nclient call and when calling to external payment, ref_no can use as idempotency\nkey from webhook received.\n6) 100M DAU -> Scalability -> Roughly calculate  we have peak 5k RPS, we scale\nmore the subscription service and payment service to handle more request, if more\nwrite needed we can use master-replica replication to handle more write on\nprimary db, if multi region -> sharding. These solutions are costly, only needed if\nmore user using.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NFR Explain : \n1) 99.99% Availability -> using db failover, cache heavy read data like subscription status, fallback again we can use db read replica\n2) Strong Consistency, CP -> use ACID transaction, fail closed if service crash/ down\n3) <100MS, check status, <200ms buy subscription p95 -> We reduce most RPC call between internal service, and we will do load test after implementing the service since latency is difficult to estimate as we have external RPC call.\n4) Durability (outbox event will make sure kafka can retry, and our worker and service will do retry after timeout)\n5) Reliability (No duplicate payment, or subscription) -> Idempotency key from client call and when calling to external payment, ref_no can use as idempotency key from webhook received.\n6) 100M DAU -> Scalability -> Roughly calculate  we have peak 5k RPS, we scale more the subscription service and payment service to handle more request, if more write needed we can use master-replica replication to handle more write on primary db, if multi region -> sharding. These solutions are costly, only needed if more user using.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ZKnbv7qw-ttGhlqpKrOq1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4759.421512068618,
      "y": 2951.166319326404,
      "width": 475.9837229470231,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1251667044,
      "version": 488,
      "versionNonce": 285617671,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795014337424,
      "created": 1794751904173,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Monitoring: cache hit rate, payment success\nrate, failed rate, duplication payment rate\n\nTesting : Load testing the concurrency to buy\nsubscription, latency to meet our NFR\n\nSecurity : JWT, if needed, encrypt the every rpc\ncall payload and response",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Monitoring: cache hit rate, payment success rate, failed rate, duplication payment rate\n\nTesting : Load testing the concurrency to buy subscription, latency to meet our NFR\n\nSecurity : JWT, if needed, encrypt the every rpc call payload and response",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CEvYvwW0PQr9jUkLOYNjk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3291.698710554854,
      "y": 912.1064727257937,
      "width": 872.2394409179688,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 174076841,
      "version": 838,
      "versionNonce": 1900248103,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795059567322,
      "created": 1795014347465,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Func Req:\n1) Risk screening before processing a payment\n2) Decides to proceed payment or reject\n3) Persist the decision\n\nNFR:\n1) 10M DAU -> 10x peak -> 115 QPS ->1157 on peak High Scalability -> DB sharding , \nno using msg broker since increase latency\n2) 100ms p99 Low latency -> move secondary important logic to async, run the important\nfirst, reduce RPC call, keep things in one monoloth as fraud detection service.\n3) 99.99% Availability -> db replication, db failover,\n4) Reliability -> idemp_key for double spending issue\n5) Durable -> \n\nCore Entites:\n1) Screening\n2) Decision\n3) Rules\nPayments\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Func Req:\n1) Risk screening before processing a payment\n2) Decides to proceed payment or reject\n3) Persist the decision\n\nNFR:\n1) 10M DAU -> 10x peak -> 115 QPS ->1157 on peak High Scalability -> DB sharding , \nno using msg broker since increase latency\n2) 100ms p99 Low latency -> move secondary important logic to async, run the important\nfirst, reduce RPC call, keep things in one monoloth as fraud detection service.\n3) 99.99% Availability -> db replication, db failover,\n4) Reliability -> idemp_key for double spending issue\n5) Durable -> \n\nCore Entites:\n1) Screening\n2) Decision\n3) Rules\nPayments\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
